{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-job-022",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 22,
  "title": "Job 22",
  "display_title": "Job 22",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "job",
  "book": "Job",
  "bookName": "Job",
  "bookOrder": 18,
  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 22,
  "sortOrder": 18022,
  "verseCount": 30,
  "aliases": [
    "Job"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:22:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Then Eliphaz the Temanite answered and said,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 22:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:22:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:22:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Can a man be profitable unto God, as he that is wise may be profitable unto himself?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 22:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:22:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:22:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "Is it any pleasure to the Almighty, that thou art righteous? or is it gain to him, that thou makest thy ways perfect?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 22:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:22:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:22:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "Will he reprove thee for fear of thee? will he enter with thee into judgment?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 22:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:22:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:22:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "Is not thy wickedness great? and thine iniquities infinite?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 22:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:22:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:22:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "For thou hast taken a pledge from thy brother for nought, and stripped the naked of their clothing.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 22:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:22:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:22:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "Thou hast not given water to the weary to drink, and thou hast withholden bread from the hungry.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 22:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:22:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:22:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "But as for the mighty man, he had the earth; and the honourable man dwelt in it.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 22:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:22:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:22:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "Thou hast sent widows away empty, and the arms of the fatherless have been broken.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 22:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:22:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:22:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "Therefore snares are round about thee, and sudden fear troubleth thee;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 22:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:22:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:22:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "Or darkness, that thou canst not see; and abundance of waters cover thee.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 22:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:22:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:22:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Is not God in the height of heaven? and behold the height of the stars, how high they are!",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 22:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:22:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:22:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "And thou sayest, How doth God know? can he judge through the dark cloud?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 22:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:22:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:22:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "Thick clouds are a covering to him, that he seeth not; and he walketh in the circuit of heaven.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 22:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:22:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:22:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "Hast thou marked the old way which wicked men have trodden?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 22:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:22:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:22:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "Which were cut down out of time, whose foundation was overflown with a flood:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 22:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:22:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:22:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "Which said unto God, Depart from us: and what can the Almighty do for them?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 22:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:22:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:22:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "Yet he filled their houses with good things: but the counsel of the wicked is far from me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 22:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:22:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:22:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "The righteous see it, and are glad: and the innocent laugh them to scorn.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 22:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:22:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:22:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "Whereas our substance is not cut down, but the remnant of them the fire consumeth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 22:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:22:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:22:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "Acquaint now thyself with him, and be at peace: thereby good shall come unto thee.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 22:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:22:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:22:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "Receive, I pray thee, the law from his mouth, and lay up his words in thine heart.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 22:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:22:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:22:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "If thou return to the Almighty, thou shalt be built up, thou shalt put away iniquity far from thy tabernacles.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 22:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:22:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:22:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "Then shalt thou lay up gold as dust, and the gold of Ophir as the stones of the brooks.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 22:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:22:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-025",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 25,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:22:25",
      "numberLabel": "25",
      "text": "Yea, the Almighty shall be thy defence, and thou shalt have plenty of silver.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 22:25",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:22:25"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-026",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 26,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:22:26",
      "numberLabel": "26",
      "text": "For then shalt thou have thy delight in the Almighty, and shalt lift up thy face unto God.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 22:26",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:22:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-027",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 27,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:22:27",
      "numberLabel": "27",
      "text": "Thou shalt make thy prayer unto him, and he shall hear thee, and thou shalt pay thy vows.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 22:27",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:22:27"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-028",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 28,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:22:28",
      "numberLabel": "28",
      "text": "Thou shalt also decree a thing, and it shall be established unto thee: and the light shall shine upon thy ways.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 22:28",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:22:28"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-029",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 29,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:22:29",
      "numberLabel": "29",
      "text": "When men are cast down, then thou shalt say, There is lifting up; and he shall save the humble person.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 22:29",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:22:29"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-030",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 30,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:22:30",
      "numberLabel": "30",
      "text": "He shall deliver the island of the innocent: and it is delivered by the pureness of thine hands.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 22:30",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:22:30"
      }
    }
  ],
